WEBVTT

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.000
It's way too oversensitive.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.320
Is this thing defective or what?

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:04.970
<b>A Flock of Hazy Moons</b>

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.640
What's wrong?

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.260
There's still time left.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.150
It's just too hard to use.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.300
That Japanese doll is a nuisance.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.890
Oh, Lt. Takamura?

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.430
There was a old Japanese doll 
in my house when I was little.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:57.610
It looked real, but it 
had the face of a corpse.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.110
I was scared of it.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.430
Don't laugh!

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.990
Even if they're both TSFs,

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:11.380
the US and Japan have completely different 
design philosophies and battle techniques,

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.290
so it's no wonder it's foreign to you.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.290
I know that.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:19.190
In that sense, the Lt.'s order that 
you pilot a Japanese practice unit

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:24.300
until the Type 94 Shiranui 
is ready was a good one.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.790
I know that too.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.400
A practice unit?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.000
Correct.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.420
You will pilot the Type 97 
practice TSF, the Fubuki,

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:41.240
until your test unit, the Shiranui is ready.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.480
Did this woman look at my record?

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:51.200
You look dissatisfied, Ensign Bridges.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:55.130
I haven't been given enough 
information to be dissatisfied.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.330
Let me ask you something.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:05.200
Is your attitude in some way related 
to your feelings about this operation?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.220
No, Liutenant.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.830
Then is it a problem with me?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.890
Not at all.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.010
Then let me say this:

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.280
your unpleasant attitude is disruptive.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.820
If you've no reason for it, fix it.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.530
Understood?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:29.990
Is that an order given as 
part of the XFJ project?

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.420
Or are you merely forcing your 
personal interests on me?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.930
Whichever you prefer.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:40.040
But fix it.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.670
I'll try. But I can't promise.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.250
Scary. Look at those two.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.490
I kind of understand how he feels.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.940
But Top Gun sure likes 
picking fights with her.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:51.820
Yeah.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.430
Even though they're both Japanese.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.010
And that's the problem.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:59.280
By the way, both Yuuya and I are Americans.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.280
Also, according to your personal data,

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:08.700
you are a second-generation 
Japanese-American, Yuuya Bridges.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.960
Yes, Lieutenant.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.960
As someone of the same race, I find that 
haughty attitude unpleasant and upsetting.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:24.130
You are, yes...

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.360
An embarrassment to the Japanese.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.520
What did she say?

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:35.510
Make sure to familiarize yourself with the 
manual for the Fubuki by the next briefing.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:36.640
Understood?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.190
I...

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.210
I'm an American.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:50.320
I was worried you were about 
to hit the Lt. back there.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.400
No way. I wouldn't hit a woman.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.160
Is that Japanese bushido?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.640
Sorry, sorry.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:00.910
But let me say this.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.580
And this goes for everything, not just TSFs.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.510
Any machine will reflect 
the mind of its creator.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.890
If you want to master a Japanese TSF,

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.020
knowing the Japanese mind 
isn't a bad place to start.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:20.830
Anyway, we've got a joint exercise 
with the Soviets tomorrow.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.080
Take 'er out for another round.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.540
Command Post to Argos Flight.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.370
Maintain present altitude and cruising speed.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.370
Course 538.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.600
600 seconds until operation start point.

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:43.290
How's the practice unit looking, Top Gun?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.230
Yeah, it's fine.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.180
That's right.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.480
I'll master any TSF, no matter what it is.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.020
Show us what you got!

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.440
It'll be fine.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.390
The goddess of victory is with you.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.640
Y-Yeah.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.080
Hey, look.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.850
The Scarlet Twins are here.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:01.650
What?

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:03.900
I'll show those girls who's boss!

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.930
Calm down, Tarisa.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.310
It's not a mock duel.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:11.360
We're just doing a joint anti-BETA exercise.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.780
Stop puffing up your chest and 
learn something from them.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:16.830
'Cause my boobs are so tiny I gotta 
puff 'em up, right? Whatever!

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.570
The Scarlet Twins.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.710
What kind of Eishi are they?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.840
I couldn't even find anything about them 
in the library of registered Eishi.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.960
Command Post to Argos Flight.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.970
Stand by at start point.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:35.590
Wide-area datalink network online.

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:36.970
Condition Red issued.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.100
JIVES online.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:54.740
There's so many!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.430
Is the system working right?

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.160
What's wrong, Top Gun?

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.030
This is pretty normal for Asia.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:02.040
Europe too.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:06.040
I guess they're used to it.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.550
Okay, mission start!

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.800
Let's do this then.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:11.470
Yeah!

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.800
Now then, what formation do we start with?

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.600
Argos 1 to all units.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.430
Approach the enemy in Arrowhead-1 formation.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.740
It's just like yesterday!

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.800
Why is it so oversensitive?

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.210
No alerts.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:39.950
Are you telling me it's working properly?

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.440
Argos 1 is surrounded.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.280
Hey, what's happened to him?

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:48.340
Mechanical trouble?

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:53.170
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.680
Present kill count is 122.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.620
You're going a little slow.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.900
Boost your kill speed by .7% percent.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.670
Roger.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:06.190
I think they're in trouble!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.480
Who?

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.200
Yuuya Bridges.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.260
Is he that green?

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:24.190
Inia, don't worry about the other squads.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:28.890
We just need to focus on the enemies 
in front of us, for the motherland.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.750
Yeah, I know.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.220
What are you playing around for?

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.120
You take the grapplers!

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.310
Right!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.240
More coming in from the southeast!

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.850
We're gonna be busy!

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.170
I was just slowing everyone down.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.530
Don't say that.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:11.770
You've barely had a chance 
to practice with it.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.590
That's not the issue.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.010
Then what is?

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:22.340
You weren't able to keep 
your Fubuki under control.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:26.530
Given that you're not used to flying it, 
a certain degree of that is forgivable.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:30.440
But if you'd understood your TSF 
better, you would have, for example,

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:34.400
chosen to make a gradual circling descent 
instead of plunging straight in.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:40.030
I'm sorry, Lt., but from my perspective 
this TSF is a piece of junk.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:40.710
Hey!

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:42.780
No, let him continue.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.350
The main engine lacks power.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.320
It's only effective at certain speeds which
 the engine has difficulty maintaining.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:54.500
And more than anything, it puts too much 
emphasis on maneuverability, making it unbalanced.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:11:00.800
But the Fubuki's no more difficult to 
control than any other Imperial Japanese TSF.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.800
I find that hard to believe.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.480
It's true.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.840
And even in the harshness of the battlefield,

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:14.240
the Imperial Japanese soldiers are 
in complete control of their TSFs.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:18.910
Even students who've not been fully trained.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:24.890
In other words, your piloting skills are 
less than those of even an Imperial trainee.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:25.830
What?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:32.370
I'll make this clear: you lack talent.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:51.630
I'll admit the TSF was working properly.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.020
You lack talent.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:01.200
But I refuse to admit that she's right.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:04.160
Are you cold?

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.060
Are you okay?

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:17.960
Yeah, I'm not that cold.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.170
No, that you got scolded.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.370
I didn't get scolded.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:30.350
I know, I'll introduce you to Misha.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.060
Misha?

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.100
That's right.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.860
Cryska and Misha.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:35.530
We're always together.

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.940
Are they your family?

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.060
Yup, my family!

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:45.620
I'm sure if you meet Misha 
you'll feel a lot better!

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:46.440
Let's go, Yuuya!

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.560
Hey, wait!

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:53.080
What happened to him, anyway?

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:56.300
Japanese TSFs don't handle like other ones.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:59.040
We'll have to help him out 
until he gets used to it.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:03.510
Well, let's go drag him out for a drink 
and give him a hard time about it.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.300
That's nice of you.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.510
You want to make him feel better?

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.260
Are you stupid?

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.090
No, I just want to make fun of him.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:15.260
I think it's a good idea. It'd 
take his mind off things?

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:21.970
What are you doing here?

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.650
Oh, don't mind me.

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:41.370
This way!

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.170
Hey.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.620
Well, if a girl like her 
can go in it's probably okay.

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.220
Yuuya, hurry!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.430
Right.

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:09.220
Um... Misha might be here.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:12.530
It opened!

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:13.990
What is this place?

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:15.660
There he is! Misha!

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:21.590
See?

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.740
I see.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.340
So that's Misha.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:29.230
Come on, Misha. Say hello to Yuuya.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.350
Hi there, Misha.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.100
Did she just say Yuuya?

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.810
Did I introduce myself?

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.650
Don't move!

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:42.220
Wait.

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:43.070
Move and I'll shoot.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:45.730
You're...

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.940
Yuuya Bridges?

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:51.070
No! Cryska!

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.920
I told you not to trust those Japs!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.620
You're wrong, dad.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.270
It's not his fault.

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.930
And I don't regret anything.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.050
How am I wrong?

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:14.970
The Japs are sly and cowardly!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.840
He used you and then threw you 
aside when you got in the way!

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.060
That's not true.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.980
And you don't know the good 
parts of the Japanese!

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.540
They're humble and polite.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:25.830
And diligent...

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:28.070
Wake up already!

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:34.190
He's half Japanese, right?

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:36.190
I heard from my grandpa

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.660
that the Japanese are cowards who 
can't do anything but sneak attacks.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.010
Let's go play somewhere else.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.500
Yeah.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.260
Hey, Mom.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.980
What?

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.760
Why does everybody avoid me?

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.950
Did I do something wrong?

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:06.650
Why does everybody avoid you?

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:13.660
Because you're an embarrassment 
to the Japanese.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.930
A dream?

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:22.920
What a horrible day.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:37.600
And an awful dream to top it all off, huh?

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.540
Anyway, who are they?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.570
Inia and Cryska?

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.690
Well, it'll work out.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:51.560
I'm sure they won't just execute me.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:54.490
I've made it this far on my own.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.660
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.830
Yes, this Takamura.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.960
<b>Prototype Type-99 EM Radiation Cannon</b>

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.680
What?

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:08.710
That idiot.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:16.720
Interrogations at this hour?

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.800
It won't take long.

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:22.180
The Soviet Union excels in 
a variety of technologies.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:25.190
But interrogations are a speciality of ours.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.560
Get off me!

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:37.230
We're going to find out what a lowly 
Japanese was doing in our top-secret facility.

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:39.440
I gave you my profile.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:40.580
I'm not Japanese.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.450
Yes, you're with the American army.

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:46.930
But you're Japanese nonetheless.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:47.800
Damn it.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.090
Even here I'm Japanese?

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.230
You're just a small island 
country in a corner of Asia.

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:55.340
You should just stay curled up there.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.430
D-Don't.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.760
Don't!

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:11.930
Excuse me.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:12.820
I'm in the middle of an interrogation.

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:15.320
But...

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:29.670
The "Why? Why?" look you had on 
your face after they let you go...

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.670
You looked like a pidgeon hit with a cannon!

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.370
The phrase is "A pidgeon 
hit with a peashooter."

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.360
That's the one!

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:38.270
Shut up, Chobi.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.410
Who are you calling Chobi?

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.060
And you smell like alcohol.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:45.850
Well, I'm glad you made it out okay.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.400
I never asked for...

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:52.740
Oh, right. It was Lt. Takamura 
who told us you were locked up.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.320
She did?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.610
She pulled some strings 
at the UN to get you out.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:19:02.120
It was probably only because I'd slow 
down the plan schedule otherwise, right?

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:08.250
But it was Tarisa who went nuts at 
Polestar saying she'd go rescue you.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:13.790
I-I told you I just wanted to laugh 
at him while we went drinking.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:19.300
I won't thank that Japanese doll.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.800
But well...

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:27.620
I know I caused trouble for you 
guys this afternoon and tonight.

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:40.870
What was that?

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.840
I couldn't hear you!

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.330
Say it louder!

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:47.730
Shut up, Chobi!

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:49.500
He's blushing!

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.080
I'm not blushing.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.550
If you want to master a Japanese TSF,

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:09.850
knowing the Japanese mind 
isn't a bad place to start.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:16.360
You're telling me of all people 
to understand the Japanese mind?

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:19.090
Looks like you made it back okay.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.570
I'm not going to thank you.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:29.950
You just don't want to lose a slave 
who can pilot your crappy TSF, right?

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:33.650
I don't care what you think about it.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:36.840
But you won't be able to get away 
with that game in a real fight.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:37.840
Game?

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.030
That mock battle.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.920
You had them protect you. 
You had them cover for you.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.740
That little game where you were 
all friends in the same Flight.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:46.100
That's fine for training, however...

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.430
Whether you can tell or not, I'm 
embarrassed by what happened today!

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.210
And you're calling it a game?

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:53.630
A situation where you know not only 
the enemy's abilities and numbers,

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:56.960
but their actions in advance.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.730
How is that not a game?

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:04.320
The BETA are beyond mankind's 
ability to predict.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.240
They don't fear death at all.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:11.250
They are tenacious and come 
in almost infinite numbers.

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:18.010
And even in a game, you blamed your machine.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:23.790
The ones who came before us managed 
to stop the BETA in even worse TSFs.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:28.470
And it's thanks to them that we can 
go and play in training exercises!

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:33.620
So these training exercises are games too?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:36.720
Then the Japanese trying to develop 
a TSF entirely on your own,

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:39.810
then having to rely on tricks 
and gimmicks to improve it...

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:41.480
That's wasn't just playing around either?

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:49.020
Hey, what happened to him?

00:21:49.020 --> 00:21:51.420
You don't need to worry about him, Inia.

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:55.500
More importantly, never hang 
out with a man like that again.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.320
Yes.

00:21:57.320 --> 00:22:01.000
We two are the only family we have.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.570
No, there's three of us.

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:04.510
Misha is here, too!

00:22:05.850 --> 00:22:07.320
Yeah.

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:10.260
It's so warm.

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:18.260
But... he really looked cold...

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:07.560
Damn it.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:10.550
Why can't I do this?

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:14.970
Nothing I tell you now 
will make a difference.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:16.620
Come on, Lieutenant.

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:18.450
I'll fight you.

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:24.440
<b>The Right Stuff</b>

00:24:19.530 --> 00:24:21.880
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:23.490
The Right Stuff.
